## Summary

**Changed file**: `src/state.rs` (111 insertions, 6 deletions)

### What changed

**1. Panic hook (lines 72-100)**: Replaced `CURRENT_MODEL_CALL_ID.with(|c| c.take())` in an `if let` pattern with a peek-before-record pattern:
• Take the ID, clone it, restore it, then record `ModelCallCompleted` while the cell is still populated
• Clear the cell explicitly after recording so the lifecycle is properly closed afterward

This eliminates the false `ModelCallCompletedWithoutStart` diagnostic that was emitted every time the panic hook closed an in-flight model call — because `record()` now sees `CURRENT_MODEL_CALL_ID` is still set when it checks.

**2. Updated test `panic_hook_closes_model_call_before_failure_observed` (line 8693)**: Matches the new peek-before-record pattern and adds an assertion that `ModelCallCompletedWithoutStart` is NOT in the event stream.

**3. New test `model_call_completed_without_start_emitted_when_no_id_active` (line 8818)**: Verifies the true-positive path — recording `ModelCallCompleted` without an active `CURRENT_MODEL_CALL_ID` correctly emits the `ModelCallCompletedWithoutStart` diagnostic.

